() Tj
T*
(1. Authority of Instructors:) Tj
T*
(Instructors have full legal and academic authority to manage the classroom environment.) Tj
T*
(Any student engaging in disruptive conduct, verbal harassment, or intentional interference) Tj
T*
(with the educational mission of PNW will be dismissed from the class session immediately.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Reporting to the Dean of Students:) Tj
T*
(Persistent disruption or repeated behavioral violations must be formally reported by the) Tj
T*
(instructor to the Office of the Dean of Students within 24 hours of occurrence.) Tj
T*
(The Dean of Students conducts an investigation under the Student Code of Conduct.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Sanctions and Appeals:) Tj
T*
(Sanctions range from written warnings, behavioral probation, mandatory counseling referrals,) Tj
T*
(to permanent suspension from Purdue University Northwest. Students maintain procedural rights) Tj
T*
(to appeal disciplinary findings through the Campus Appeals Committee.) Tj
T*
